From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0280: Bluetooth phase 1: WCN3988 UART on QUP0 SE3

A first look at the Bluetooth controller (research/bluetooth.md, phase 1). New
bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c, nothing runs at boot:
  kern.sweet_bt = 1: RPM votes for L9/L16/L17/L23 (shared with Wi-Fi and the
    fingerprint sensor: never turned off), the SE3 clocks (GCC vote 0x7900c bit
    13, CBCR 0x1f4d4, RCG 0x1f4d8, read from gcc-khaje.ko; each register logged
    before it is written), then SE3's FW_REVISION: protocol (bits 15:8) must be 2
    (UART) before anything else is touched. Then GPIO 8-11 to qup3 (function 1 in
    pinctrl-khaje.ko, eGPIO bit kept), the SE clock rate (a DFS level that fits,
    else the RCG at 7.3728 MHz) and the GENI UART in FIFO mode, polled, 115200
    8N1 with RTS/CTS.
  = 2: the power pulse (0xFC at 2400 baud, no flow control), back to 115200,
    HCI_Reset (expects 04 0E 04 01 03 0C 00) and EDL_PATCH_VER_REQ (0xFC00 sub-op
    0x19), every reply byte logged.
  = 3: HCI_Read_Local_Version and HCI_Read_BD_ADDR.
  = 9: the UART stopped; the rails stay voted.
kern.sweet_bt_log holds the last request's log (also in the kernel log).
/dev/qcabt (made at op 1): raw H4 bytes both ways, a polling thread fills an
8 KB ring only while the node is open. Every wait is bounded.
 bsd/conf/files     |   1 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c | 797 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 798 insertions(+)

